  "rule": "For each candidate: RMSE on each of the four recipe months versus the incumbent's development prediction, and the pooled twelve-month residual-scope RMSE of its residual mean versus the control's (the incumbent's mean of adj2 and cat on the same rows). Eligible when not worse on ANY recipe month (ratio <= 1.0), mean ratio over the four recipe months at most 0.9998 (0.02%), the paired-day bootstrap interval of the RMSE difference below zero on every recipe month where the candidate differs from the baseline on at least one row, and the pooled residual-scope RMSE strictly below the control's. Choose the eligible candidate with the lowest mean ratio over the four recipe months (ties by name); otherwise select nothing and keep v23. repro is a check and cannot be selected. Per-airport, ordinary-row and per-month scope figures are descriptive.",
